{"doc_id": "6883f999d3f384b2a9a3e625", "initial_prompt": "<image>\nLook at some of my old receipts in the image. Tell me the total tax I paid for the purchases shown, mentioning the tax paid for each purchase. What was the subtotal for the Canadian Tire receipt for the repair order? If the subtotal was calculated after a store-wide 20% discount was applied, what was the original total price before the discount and tax were applied?", "ground_truth": "After flipping the image horizontally, it is possible to identify the tax paid on each purchase:\nReceipt 1 (far left): A debit card purchase with a tax of $13.00.\n\nReceipt 2 (center, Canadian Tire): A debit card purchase with a tax of $8.58. \n\nReceipt 3 (bottom right): A purchase with a tax of $26.00.\n\nReceipt 4 (top): A purchase with a tax of $35.75.\n\nTotal Tax Paid = $13 + $8.58 + $26 + $35.75 = $83.33\n\nThe original price of the Canadian tire repair order after the discount is $65.99, so the original total price before the discount and tax was $82.49.\n\nThis is because 65.99/(1−0.20)=$82.49."}
